[{"content":"You are editing one repository copy in /workspace. Read instruction.md and use the repository tools to implement and check the feature. Call submit_output when finished; the files are the submission. Give a summary and your own assessment of completion, checks performed, and remaining work. Hidden checks and reference answers are unavailable. Do not use network access or install packages.","role":"system"},{"content":"# Task\n\n# Compile a pass-through stage\n\nThe workflow compiler already handles delegated sessions and repository\nprovisioning. Add a built-in `pass_through` stage type to the existing dispatch\narchitecture. Its configuration is exactly an empty JSON object; reject any\nother configuration with a stage-scoped compile error. It materializes as one\nscalar unit, releases every declared output immediately, and preserves the\nempty configuration in the compiled executor contract. Existing stage types,\ncustom injected compiler registries, and attention validation must keep their\ncurrent behavior.\n\nThe public checks are `bun test ./tests/visible` and\n`tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`. The evaluator also runs private feature and\nregression checks. Keep the implementation within the existing source tree.\n\n## Workspace\n\nThe repository is your working directory, `/workspace`. Edit its files in place; the file tree you leave there is your submission. Call `submit_output` with a short summary when you are done.\n","role":"user"},{"content":"# Writable scope\n\nCreate, modify, or delete files only under these directory prefixes:\n- src/compiler/\n\nAll other paths are read-only, including visible tests and dependency and configuration files outside the allowed prefixes. An edit outside this scope rejects the submission.\n\n# Budget\n\n900 seconds; at most 60 model requests; at most 8192 output tokens per request.","role":"user"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"path\":\"instruction.md\",\"start_l